  "title": "Загриженост во бременост или по породување",
  "summary_en": "Pregnancy and postpartum concerns. Seizure, heavy bleeding, severe abdominal pain, pre-eclampsia features, chest pain/breathlessness → 194. Reduced/absent fetal movements, waters breaking, regular contractions <37 weeks, fever, severe vomiting, calf swelling → same day (go now) to maternity. Itching of hands/feet → 24–48h. Postpartum: heavy bleeding, fever, wound infection, mood (crisis → global crisis).",
  "notes_en": "NHS pregnancy pages: reduced movements, waters breaking, bleeding, pre-eclampsia, severe vomiting, labour signs; postnatal danger signs (bleeding, fever, DVT, mood/psychosis). Cord prolapse knee-chest position is standard public first aid. Status: draft — awaiting clinician review („нацрт — чека лекарски преглед“).",
